  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "$2{b}^{3}(-\\frac{b}{4}+{b}^{3}-\\frac{1}{3})=${{field-1}}\n$\\,-$\n{{field-2}}${b}^{3}$",
  "worked_solution": "We multiply each term inside the parentheses by the term outside the parentheses, simplify using the rules of exponents, and then we add the results together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{b}^{3}(-\\frac{b}{4}+{b}^{3}-\\frac{1}{3}) & = \\\\ 2{b}^{3}\\cdot (-\\frac{b}{4})+2{b}^{3}\\cdot {b}^{3}+2{b}^{3}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{3}) & = \\\\ (-\\frac{1}{2})({b}^{3+1})+2({b}^{3+3})+(-\\frac{2}{3}){b}^{3} & = \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}{b}^{4}+2{b}^{6}-\\frac{2}{3}{b}^{3} & = \\\\ 2{b}^{6}-\\frac{1}{2}{b}^{4}-\\frac{2}{3}{b}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
